From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kel Modderman <kelvmod@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 09:10:00 +1000
Subject: media: qcom: iris: Do not flag the empty LAST buffer as an error

The gen2 firmware ends a source change with an empty capture buffer
flagged HFI_BUF_FW_FLAG_PSC_LAST. iris_hfi_gen2_handle_output_buffer()
flags empty buffers that are not HFI_BUF_FW_FLAG_LAST with
V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR while streaming, so this buffer is one of them.
iris_vb2_buffer_done() returns early for error buffers, before the LAST
handling, so no EOS event is queued, the m2m context is not marked
stopped and inst->last_buffer_dequeued stays false.

A capture buffer queued between that LAST buffer and the client's
V4L2_DEC_CMD_START is then returned by iris_vb2_buf_queue() as a second
empty LAST buffer. The client's START after the first LAST buffer clears
the stop, dequeuing the second sets vb2's last_buffer_dequeued again,
START now fails with EBUSY and VIDIOC_DQBUF returns EPIPE from then on.
Kodi with ffmpeg's v4l2m2m decoder froze the picture after a few seeks
on a Radxa Dragon Q6A.

An empty LAST buffer only ends a drain or a source change and carries
no picture, so clear the error flag and let the LAST handling run.
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_buffer.c
@@ -894,6 +894,10 @@
 
 	vb2 = &vbuf->vb2_buf;
 
+	/* an empty LAST buffer ends a drain or source change, not an error */
+	if (buf->flags & V4L2_BUF_FLAG_LAST && !buf->data_size)
+		buf->flags &= ~V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR;
+
 	vbuf->flags |= buf->flags;
 
 	if (buf->flags & V4L2_BUF_FLAG_ERROR) {
